 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Hit rates and miss rates alone do not say how fast memory feels. AMAT, the average memory access time, does, and it is the most asked memory question in GATE."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "AMAT"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The formula and its two conventions, units, and where the miss penalty comes from."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then two cache levels, split caches, turning AMAT into CPI, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[3..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "formula",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: every access pays the hit time. Misses also pay the miss penalty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: the formula"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So AMAT equals hit time, plus miss rate times miss penalty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "f[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Example: a 4 nanosecond cache, 10 percent misses, and 20 nanosecond memory. 4 plus 0.1 times 20 is 6 nanoseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "f[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "f[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Picture it. A hit takes 4 nanoseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "f"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tl"
      },
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "tl",
       "id": "h",
       "lane": "hit",
       "start": 0,
       "end": 4,
       "label": "L1 4"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Usually a miss first looks in the cache, fails, then goes to memory: 4 plus 20, 24 nanoseconds. This is hierarchical, or look-through, access."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "tl",
       "id": "s1",
       "lane": "miss: L1 first, then memory",
       "start": 0,
       "end": 4,
       "label": "L1 4"
      },
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "tl",
       "id": "s2",
       "lane": "miss: L1 first, then memory",
       "start": 4,
       "end": 24,
       "label": "memory 20",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Some designs start memory at the same time as the cache. Then a miss costs just the memory time, 20."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "add_block",
       "target": "tl",
       "id": "p1",
       "lane": "miss: L1 and memory together",
       "start": 0,
       "end": 20,
       "label": "memory 20, L1 checked alongside"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "That is the second convention, and the formula changes: hit fraction times 4, plus miss fraction times 20, which is 5.6."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "tl"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "f"
      },
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "f[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "f[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "GATE says which one it means. Hierarchical, look-through, or no word at all: the miss pays both. Simultaneous or parallel: the miss pays memory only."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "f"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "conv"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "conv[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Note the first formula simplifies: h times t1, plus 1 minus h times t1 plus t2, is just t1 plus the miss rate times t2. The same as hit time plus miss rate times penalty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "conv[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And the parallel one does not."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "conv[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "look-through: t₁ + (1 − h)·t₂ · simultaneous: h·t₁ + (1 − h)·t₂"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "units",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: keep the units the same. Here the hit time is in cycles, but memory is given in nanoseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: cycles or nanoseconds"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "conv"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "cy"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "At 2 gigahertz a cycle is 0.5 nanoseconds, so 50 nanoseconds of memory is 100 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cy[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With a 1 cycle hit and 5 percent misses, AMAT is 1 plus 0.05 times 100: 6 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "cy[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cy[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And 6 cycles is 3 nanoseconds. Convert once, at the start or the end, never in the middle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "cy[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cy[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "pick one unit: convert ns ↔ cycles with the clock period"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "penalty",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: sometimes you must build the miss penalty yourself. A block is 4 words. Sending the address takes 1 cycle, each memory access 15 cycles, and each word transfer 1 cycle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: building the miss penalty"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "cy"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "mp"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With memory one word wide and one bank, the 4 words are read one after another: 1 plus 4 times 15 plus 4 times 1, which is 65 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mp[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mp[0][4]",
       "value": "1 + 60 + 4 = 65",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 4 interleaved banks, all 4 words are read at once, in one 15 cycle access, then sent one per cycle: 1 plus 15 plus 4, just 20 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mp[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "mp[1][4]",
       "value": "1 + 15 + 4 = 20",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With a 5 percent miss rate, AMAT falls from 4.25 to 2 cycles, with the same DRAM chips."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "mpx"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "mpx[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: the address is sent once, but the transfer cost is paid for every word. Count each part."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "mpx"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "penalty = address + access(es) + transfers · interleaving overlaps the accesses"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "two",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: two levels. L1 takes 1 cycle and misses 4 percent of the time. L2 takes 10 cycles and misses half of what reaches it. Memory takes 200."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: L1 and L2"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "mp"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hier"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hier[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hier[1]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The trick: L1's miss penalty is itself an AMAT, the AMAT of L2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "hier"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "two"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "two[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So: 1 plus 0.04 times, 10 plus 0.5 times 200."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "two[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "two[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "10 plus 100 is 110. 0.04 times 110 is 4.4. AMAT is 5.4 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "two[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "two[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now the trap. That 50 percent is the local miss rate of L2: misses divided by the accesses that reach L2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "two"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "lg"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lg[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Out of 1000 CPU accesses, 40 miss in L1 and reach L2, and 20 of those miss again. Local: 20 over 40, 50 percent."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lg[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The global miss rate divides by all 1000 CPU accesses: 2 percent. It says what fraction of all accesses go to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lg[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "They are linked: global equals the L1 miss rate times the local L2 miss rate. Use the local rate inside the AMAT formula."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lg[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "AMAT uses the LOCAL L2 miss rate · global = MR₁ × local MR₂"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: most processors have separate instruction and data caches. Each instruction makes 1 fetch, and here 0.3 data accesses."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 7: split I- and D-caches"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "lg"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "split"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "split[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So of every 1.3 accesses, 1 goes to the instruction cache and 0.3 to the data cache: weights of 0.77 and 0.23."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "split[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "split[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The I-cache misses 1 percent, the D-cache 4 percent, with a 100 cycle penalty: AMATs of 2 and 5 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "split[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "split[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The combined AMAT weights them: 0.77 times 2 plus 0.23 times 5, about 2.69 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "split[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "split[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: do not just average 2 and 5. There are more than three instruction fetches for every data access."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "weight each cache by its share of accesses"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cpi",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: from AMAT to CPI. Every miss stalls the processor, and those stall cycles add to the CPI."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 7: from AMAT to CPI"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "split"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
